WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:13.539
Once upon a time, there lived a married couple who desperately wanted to have a child.

2
00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:16.440
Their house overlooked a beautiful garden.

3
00:00:17.261 --> 00:00:21.543
Every day from her window, the wife looked down at all the flowers and herbs.

4
00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:24.125
Her favorite was the rapunzel herb.

5
00:00:24.145 --> 00:00:29.968
"If only I had a daughter as beautiful as that rapunzel," she wished.

6
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.701
Finally the wife became pregnant.

7
00:00:34.681 --> 00:00:40.783
One day the wife, pointing to the rapunzel, asked her husband, "Darling, would you bring me some of

8
00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:41.463
those herbs?"

9
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:46.925
"But but that's the witch's garden," he stammered.

10
00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:50.526
"If I don't have some rapunzel, I'll die!"

11
00:00:51.106 --> 00:00:52.006
she said angrily.

12
00:00:53.126 --> 00:00:55.027
Everyone was afraid of the old witch.

13
00:00:56.107 --> 00:00:58.688
She had great powers and cast spells on people.

14
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.222
No one dared enter her garden, knowing they would probably not come out alive!

15
00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:08.385
The wife refused to eat anything and began to look pale.

16
00:01:09.505 --> 00:01:13.908
Worrying about her health, as well as the baby's, the husband finally gave in.

17
00:01:13.928 --> 00:01:16.889
"I'll get the herbs for you," he said.

18
00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.931
"Thank you, honey," she said.

19
00:01:20.751 --> 00:01:22.813
She blew him a kiss and clapped her hands.

20
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:28.716
That night the husband crept into the witch's garden and stole some rapunzel.

21
00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:32.445
He brought it to his wife, who immediately ate it up.

22
00:01:33.586 --> 00:01:35.707
"Bring me fresh rapunzel every night!"

23
00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:37.107
she said happily.

24
00:01:38.588 --> 00:01:45.871
For a few nights after that, the husband bravely did as his wife asked until one evening, when

25
00:01:45.891 --> 00:01:47.692
he got caught by the witch herself.

26
00:01:47.712 --> 00:01:51.754
"So you are the thief stealing my rapunzel!"

27
00:01:52.794 --> 00:01:53.955
she accused angrily.

28
00:01:53.975 --> 00:01:56.916
"Please have mercy," he pleaded.

29
00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:00.593
"My pregnant wife said she would die if she couldn't have some."

30
00:02:03.174 --> 00:02:07.415
"Take as much as you like," the witch said, softening her voice.

31
00:02:07.435 --> 00:02:12.736
"But in return, the child born to you will be mine!"

32
00:02:13.316 --> 00:02:17.518
The husband, frightened out of his wits, had no choice but to agree.

33
00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:21.499
A few months later, a baby girl was born.

34
00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:28.301
The couple's happiness lasted only a short time because soon after, the witch appeared.

35
00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:35.423
She snatched the baby from the astonished wife and said, "I will call her Rapunzel and raise her

36
00:02:35.563 --> 00:02:36.363
as my own."

37
00:02:37.764 --> 00:02:41.445
Without another word, she vanished, taking Rapunzel with her.

38
00:02:42.705 --> 00:02:45.666
Rapunzel grew up to be an extremely beautiful girl.

39
00:02:46.986 --> 00:02:51.748
The witch did not want others to see her beauty, so she shut Rapunzel up in a tower.

40
00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.114
This tower, located in the forest, had no stairs or doors.

41
00:02:57.035 --> 00:02:59.016
There was only one way to enter it.

42
00:03:00.057 --> 00:03:01.698
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel!

43
00:03:01.978 --> 00:03:03.499
Let down your hair!"

44
00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.340
shouted the witch.

45
00:03:07.041 --> 00:03:09.703
From the small window dropped a thick golden rope.

46
00:03:10.764 --> 00:03:14.406
The witch climbed up the strange, shiny rope to the top of the tower.

47
00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:17.588
But in fact, it was no rope at all.

48
00:03:18.684 --> 00:03:22.865
Rapunzel had magnificent, long golden hair that reached past her feet.

49
00:03:23.846 --> 00:03:27.907
Whenever the witch called out, Rapunzel dropped her hair out the window.

50
00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:33.348
A few years later, the king's son happened to be riding through the forest.

51
00:03:34.128 --> 00:03:37.369
He imagined that he heard an angel singing and stopped to listen.

52
00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:40.630
"No, it's the voice of a maiden!"

53
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:41.931
he realized.

54
00:03:42.971 --> 00:03:46.552
The sweet melancholy voice was coming from a tower just ahead.

55
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:53.103
Upon seeing Rapunzel in the window, the prince fell deeply in love with her.

56
00:03:54.044 --> 00:03:56.545
He longed to go up and declare his feelings to her.

57
00:03:56.565 --> 00:04:00.268
"But how can I get inside that tower?"

58
00:04:01.789 --> 00:04:03.250
He was about to find out.

59
00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.752
He saw the witch approach the tower.

60
00:04:05.772 --> 00:04:08.714
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel!

61
00:04:09.074 --> 00:04:10.555
Let down your hair!"

62
00:04:11.075 --> 00:04:11.856
shouted the witch.

63
00:04:13.457 --> 00:04:17.920
The prince watched in amazement as a long golden rope descended from the window.

64
00:04:18.948 --> 00:04:24.790
The prince waited until the witch left and then called out loudly, "Rapunzel, Rapunzel!

65
00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.290
Let down your hair!"

66
00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:31.332
A few minutes later, the rope appeared, and the prince began his climb.

67
00:04:33.692 --> 00:04:38.374
Rapunzel was shocked when she saw a strange man enter through the tower window.

68
00:04:38.394 --> 00:04:42.235
"I mean no harm," the prince spoke gently.

69
00:04:43.135 --> 00:04:46.356
He confessed his feelings for her and asked if she would marry him.

70
00:04:47.324 --> 00:04:51.006
Rapunzel's heart welled with joy, and she accepted his proposal.

71
00:04:52.007 --> 00:04:54.688
Rapunzel and the prince continued to meet secretly.

72
00:04:55.969 --> 00:04:58.590
On each visit, the prince brought some silk threads.

73
00:04:59.691 --> 00:05:03.753
Rapunzel used the silk to make a rope so she could escape from the tower.

74
00:05:03.773 --> 00:05:06.615
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel!

75
00:05:06.975 --> 00:05:08.656
Let down your hair!"

76
00:05:09.436 --> 00:05:11.417
shouted the witch at her usual time.

77
00:05:12.398 --> 00:05:18.837
As she let her hair fall down, Rapunzel thought happily to herself that today would be her last

78
00:05:18.897 --> 00:05:19.897
day as a captive.

79
00:05:20.898 --> 00:05:27.961
In a few hours, the prince would come on his horse and "What are you so happy about?"

80
00:05:28.481 --> 00:05:30.562
The witch interrupted Rapunzel's thoughts.

81
00:05:31.882 --> 00:05:35.164
"Uh nothing," Rapunzel stammered.

82
00:05:36.404 --> 00:05:37.285
"What's that?"

83
00:05:38.145 --> 00:05:40.426
The witch pointed to something next to the bed.

84
00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:45.088
Rapunzel stared in horror as the witch held up the prince's hat.

85
00:05:46.624 --> 00:05:48.105
"Ungrateful girl!

86
00:05:48.345 --> 00:05:50.046
You dare deceive me?"

87
00:05:50.626 --> 00:05:52.928
yelled the witch.

88
00:05:52.948 --> 00:05:54.389
"I I love him!

89
00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:56.530
We're going to get married!"

90
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.771
Rapunzel managed to reply.

91
00:05:59.952 --> 00:06:03.454
The witch's eyes turned red as she pulled out a pair of scissors.

92
00:06:04.695 --> 00:06:10.098
Then in the blink of an eye—snip, snip!—Rapunzel's braid fell to the floor.

93
00:06:11.058 --> 00:06:13.600
The witch then banished Rapunzel to the forest.

94
00:06:15.376 --> 00:06:19.059
That evening the prince arrived, unaware of what had happened.

95
00:06:19.079 --> 00:06:21.541
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel!

96
00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:22.963
Let down your hair!"

97
00:06:23.403 --> 00:06:24.684
he called out joyfully.

98
00:06:25.745 --> 00:06:27.927
The end of the braid fell and hit his head.

99
00:06:27.947 --> 00:06:31.510
"Ouch!" The prince rubbed his head.

100
00:06:32.431 --> 00:06:35.173
Climbing the tower, he thought only of getting married.

101
00:06:36.154 --> 00:06:40.157
"Tonight will be the last time I Suddenly he screamed.

102
00:06:41.298 --> 00:06:43.420
Looking out the window at him was the witch.

103
00:06:44.656 --> 00:06:46.057
The prince was speechless.

104
00:06:46.077 --> 00:06:50.618
"So you tried to steal what's not yours!"

105
00:06:51.438 --> 00:06:52.959
said the witch, moving closer.

106
00:06:53.959 --> 00:06:58.460
Before she could cast a spell on him, the prince let go of Rapunzel's hair.

107
00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.141
He fell into a thorny bush that pierced his eyes.

108
00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:06.643
Blinded, the prince got on his horse and took off for the forest.

109
00:07:07.723 --> 00:07:10.524
Days turned to weeks, and weeks turned to months.

110
00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.342
The blind prince searched and searched for his beloved.

111
00:07:15.382 --> 00:07:17.343
He could find no trace of Rapunzel.

112
00:07:18.444 --> 00:07:24.247
After several years the prince was about to give up and return to his palace when he heard

113
00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:25.508
a familiar sound.

114
00:07:25.528 --> 00:07:28.169
"Rapunzel? Is that you?"

115
00:07:29.129 --> 00:07:31.571
he called out toward the sweet singing voice.

116
00:07:32.711 --> 00:07:35.833
The singing stopped abruptly, and the woman turned around.

117
00:07:35.853 --> 00:07:40.155
"My prince, you found me!"

118
00:07:40.716 --> 00:07:41.276
she cried.

119
00:07:42.256 --> 00:07:46.760
As tears of joy ran down his face, the prince saw a bright light.

120
00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:49.403
True love reopened his eyes.

121
00:07:50.364 --> 00:07:53.306
Not even the witch's hate could separate them forever.

122
00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:59.072
The prince took Rapunzel back to his palace, and they lived happily ever after.
